Local accepted the shape of the table: billing mode, the on-demand maximum, both indexes (including the three-attribute `byMerchant` key), the stream and deletion protection, which then refused the `delete-table`. It accepted the warm throughput but reports `null`, because there's nothing to warm in one process. Point-in-time recovery is an unknown operation: the docs list it as unsupported in Local. TTL is accepted; in my run an item that had expired ten minutes earlier was still there, so don't use Local to test when TTL deletes happen.
